                <pb facs="0800" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">791.003/76: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-05T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Your 21, March 5, 11 a.m., paragraph (4). The Department presumes you were
                    referring to political aims of Great Britain and that you approve cooperation
                    with the British on a basis of the 16 safeguards to protect foreigners in Persia
                    following abrogation of the treaties. Please cable a reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
